Sources consulted, not copied: the XTDB paper (Sundman et al., Calphad 90 (2025) 102849,
CC BY-NC) and the XTDB documentation at https://github.com/sundmanbo/XTDB (GPL-3.0,
documents and example databases) were read to write src/xtdb.c and
python/mqmqa/utdb_xtdb.py. No text, code or data from them is included here.
Sundman, Calphad 15 (1991) 109-119, was read to write the SUBI (ionic liquid) reader in
src/cs_dat.c; no text from it is included. Pelton, Calphad 12 (1988) 127-142, and Kaye,
Lewis and Thompson, J. Nucl. Mater. 366 (2007) 8-27, were read to write the QKTO reader;
no text from them is included. pycalphad's pycalphad/core/calculate.py and
pycalphad/core/workspace.py were opened to read the default sampling density of its
equilibrium call for validation/fig4_comparison; no code from them is included.

Hephaestus contains code translated from third-party software. Each source keeps its
license and copyright notice, reproduced below. Which files are affected is listed in the
Provenance section of README.md.

