The Hermes tab of web/index.html runs, unchanged, Hermes 0.3.0
(https://github.com/odinzen/hermes, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23923573; MIT, copyright
Nigel Lee En Hew and Odinzen LLC, licence text in web/hermes/LICENSE-hermes.txt). The
wheel web/hermes/hermes-0.3.0-py3-none-any.whl is built from the v0.3.0 release commit, and
web/hermes/fe3pt_demo.npz is every fourth volume of the Fe3Pt example data in that
release's tests/test_data/Fe3Pt_three_configs.pkl. Hermes's configuration.py and system.py
were read for its API; web/hermes_worker.js calls Hermes and copies no code from it.

The tab runs on Pyodide 0.28.3 (MPL-2.0, https://pyodide.org) with its numpy (BSD-3-Clause),
scipy (BSD-3-Clause) and OpenBLAS (BSD-3-Clause) builds, packaging (Apache-2.0 or
BSD-2-Clause), plotly 7.1.0 (MIT) and narwhals 2.29.0 (MIT). scripts/build_hermes_web.py
fetches these into web/vendor/pyodide/ with pinned checksums; they are not tracked in git,
and each keeps its own licence.
